Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||04:19 PM||||What I did, was download each GIF image onto my own computer here(by right-clicking on the red "x-box" and selecting properties- it shows the exact web location), then used PIP to upload them to the PFF upload directory.  I then altered the address to point to the new file location (which is the <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/*title*.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/*title*.gif</A>  address).  The *title* spot is intended just for the simple filename, like 666.gif for the odometer.  So the imageline for the odometer is {img}http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/666.gif{/img} again, where {} are changed to []  so you'll see this:   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/666.gif">  <P>Does that help, or did I just make it worse?<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||tomanyfieros||10-25-2001||04:27 PM||||on the mailing list, there was a guy that sent one out about his fiero, it went something like this<BR>i wsa drving out on the backroads, and my car started to dye on me, so i pulled over and it would not start (or something like that) and he sat there waiting on a car to pass by to flag down and get a ride. (and it was night time) and he said he saw some lights that were pop ups, and whe nthe car went by, it was a black GT, and it stopped. this girl that was driving the GT asked if he needed help, and he asked her to take him to the gas station that was close. she took him there and when he got out, she pulled away and he got the plate #, he talked to his friend and got the address (the guy worked at the motor bruero or what ever) and he called and called, and could not get anyone to answer. so one day he went out to Thank her for the help aand stuff. he went out there and when he pulled in to the driveway, a old lady was sitting there, and he went up to her and asked if (i dont remember the name) was there, and she started crying. he said "here name" and said she gave him a ride home... the o.l. started crying even more and asked him if it was a joke. he said no. the o.l. said that she died 3 years ago in a car crash, (and it was in the fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ) he said he was sorry and when he was leaving, he backed up to this barn that was the o.l.'s barn, and could barely see in there, and there sat the GT that he rode in, and it was torn to pieces from the crash (aka hit hard, not torn down) and he never went back.....<BR>i heard this like a yr ago on the mailing list.... i had a dream i was that guy and it was strange..... i will have to draw a picture of this.... a lolc (little old ladies car, grandma's 99 caddy fully optioned plate name! hers is lolc13) anyways... thought i would help out in this topic.... anyone still have that email of this? i liked the story, untill i got to the part the fiero was wrecked..... Thanx Jason <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
